{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He rebukes and it dries up</b> — it lacks a yod so that two yods do not come together, and it is from the heavy stem with a dagesh. תיבש is the cause, for just as one says from יאבד, ויאבדם, so it was fitting to say ויבשהו — only it would not be seemly for two yods to be joined. And now he recounts the power of HaShem over sea and dry land, that there is none who can stand before Him." "<b>And the meaning of 'the Bashan languishes'</b> — on account of 'and all the rivers He dried up.' And this matter, that He dried up the rivers, on account of the withholding of rain from upon the earth — this matter caused the Bashan and the Carmel to languish, of every fruit of produce."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "I read תיבש as referring to the causative form; the sentence is compressed and the precise grammatical argument is cryptic. I translate hyper-literally without expanding.", 1 "Resolved הגשם as 'the rain' (הַגֶּשֶׁם) rather than 'the body'; the context of drought and vegetation supports this reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:30.146122222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}